From: Fabien Danieau <fabien.danieau@pollen-robotics.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2: enable uart2 for the motor bus

CONFIG_FIQ_DEBUGGER=n frees the driver but not the hardware: Rockchip's
rk3568-linux.dtsi leaves &uart2 disabled and assigns UART2 to its fiq_debugger
node, so disabling the debugger in the kernel config alone yields neither
ttyFIQ0 nor ttyS2. Enable &uart2 on the m0 pins and disable the fiq_debugger
node, matching radxa's rk3568-uart2-m0.dts overlay.

Only applied when MICRODUCK_MOTOR_UART = "1"; see
conf/machine/include/microduck-common.inc.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2.dts
@@ -56,6 +56,34 @@
 	status = "okay";
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart1m0_xfer &uart1m0_ctsn>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * Hand UART2 to robotd's Dynamixel bus.
+ *
+ * Turning CONFIG_FIQ_DEBUGGER off (motorbus.cfg) is necessary and NOT sufficient.
+ * Rockchip's rk3568-linux.dtsi leaves &uart2 status = "disabled" and gives the
+ * hardware to its fiq_debugger node instead, so with the driver gone nothing
+ * drives UART2 at all. Measured on the board 2026-09-11, kernel config alone:
+ * /dev/ttyFIQ0 correctly disappeared, /dev/ttyS2 never appeared, fe660000.serial
+ * was not even a platform device, and robotd sat in its retry loop exactly as
+ * before. Only fe650000.serial (uart1) had bound dw-apb-uart.
+ *
+ * m0 pins, and disabling fiq_debugger rather than deleting it, both follow
+ * radxa's own rk3568-uart2-m0.dts overlay -- whose compatible list includes
+ * radxa,zero3, and which their setup-board.sh enables as "uart2-m0" on the
+ * Armbian prototype this board replaces.
+ *
+ * By path, not &fiq_debugger: Armbian's rk3568-linux.dtsi drops that label.
+ */
+&{/fiq-debugger} {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&uart2 {
+	status = "okay";
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&uart2m0_xfer>;
 };
 
 &sdmmc1 {
